    "result_text": "The only test class (`AcceptanceTest`) is the full suite, and all tests pass. BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` business rule: **SILVER** when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise **BRONZE**.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` string property (enum `SILVER`/`BRONZE`) to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator produces the field (and `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum`) on the DTO served by `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Named(\"formatMembershipTier\")` method wired via `@Mapping(... qualifiedByName = \"formatMembershipTier\")`, following the same pattern as the other derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`). It returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` and the email is non-empty, otherwise `BRONZE` (null-safe for both inputs).\n\n`namesakeCount` is always populated on create (`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`), so the field is deterministic at read time. All tests pass (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS).",
